2. biochemical examination: ALB ≥ 29 g / L (AlB did not lose within 14 days); ALT and AST \ 150mmHg, diastolic blood pressure\>100mmHg); patients with grade Ⅱ or more myocardial ischemia or myocardial infarction, poorly controlled arrhythmia (including QTC interval≥450ms) and Ⅲ\~Ⅳ grade cardiac insufficiency according to NYHA; cardiac color Doppler ultrasonography: LVEF \ 16 s, APTT\>43 s, TT\>21 s, Fbg \<2 g/L), hemorrhagic tendency or receiving thrombolysis or anticoagulant therapy;
