8. Good organ and bone marrow function, defined as follows:

Hematologic System (No blood transfusions or treatment with hematopoietic growth factors within the past 14 days)
* Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC) ≥ 1.5×10⁹/L
* Platelets (PLT) ≥ 100×10⁹/L
* Hemoglobin (Hb) ≥ 90 g/L Liver Function
* Total Bilirubin (TBIL) ≤ 1.5×ULN (For patients with Gilbert's syndrome: ≤ 3×ULN)
* Alanine Aminotransferase (ALT) ≤ 2.5×ULN (Patients with liver metastases: ≤ 5×ULN)
* Aspartate Aminotransferase (AST) ≤ 2.5×ULN (Patients with liver metastases: ≤ 5×ULN)
* Albumin (ALB) ≥ 30 g/L Renal Function
